  "body": "We would like a way to trace a well defined subset of all traces. This would include any traces related to member of the core matrix.org team. Though this is supposedly supported by [jaeger-client-python](https://github.com/jaegertracing/jaeger-client-python#programmatically) however it seems to be borked: \r\n![Screenshot from 2019-07-18 17-07-50](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23084468/61812491-82aa1980-ae3b-11e9-82c6-2a9ec6391d0b.png)\r\n\r\nI've just started a conversation [with the jaeger dev team](https://matrix.to/#/!MoumXuDqciyqwHizTS:matrix.org/$156398634660283joNff:matrix.org?via=matrix.org&via=half-shot.uk).\r\n\r\nWe may consider another tracer. However, many of the implementations do not support this.\r\n\r\nThe above photo comes from the attempted implementation in /matrix-org/synapse/tree/joriks/opentracing_span_conscription",
